    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (the others are a base and a helper), and the full `mvn test` run compiled everything and ran it green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `customerCode` assignment for `POST /api/owners`, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persistent `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`). Tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column is required for the field to persist and read back.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps `Owner.customerCode \u2192 OwnerDto.customerCode` by name (surfacing it on `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\n4. **New pipeline step** (`function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 mutates the built `Owner` in place: `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, `NNNN` = `String.format(\"%04d\", ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1)` (one more than the current owner count).\n\n5. **Endpoint wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted `assignCustomerCode` between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance, so the count reflects already-persisted owners and each new owner takes the next number in the global sequence.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test confirms `smithers \u2192 SMI-\u2026`, `jones \u2192 JON-\u2026`, and that the second owner's number is exactly one greater than the first's.",
